From c03c34d598582b80dbd9250c89da1871a8aa0d3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Zero <sasha@ripostelabs.xyz>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:32:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add H.264 CAVLC q_sign feature to ffedit

Export and re-apply the sign of every residual coefficient as the
"q_sign" feature: one 0/1 per non-zero level of each macroblock, in
the order decode_residual() reads them. Intra macroblocks have no
motion vectors, so the mv features left every I-frame untouched; the
signs reach them.

Only the sign moves. |level| is kept, so coeff_token, total_zeros,
run_before and the suffixLength adaptation do not change and the slot
layout is fixed by the input stream. A trailing_ones_sign_flag is one
bit; any other sign is the parity of levelCode, and put_level() is
the 9.2.2.1 encoder (prefix 14 and 15 suffixes, the >= 16 escape, the
levelCode - 2 rule for the first level after fewer than three trailing
ones). Its code length changes only in the bare unary case, which the
existing NAL rebuild handles.

decode_residual() records each level's bit offset and suffixLength and
calls ffe_h264_levels() once per block. ffe_h264_mb_start() now takes
the decoder context and flushes the previous macroblock's signs to the
JSON; ffe_h264_nal_done() flushes the last one. FFEditH264Edit gained
a kind (se(v), raw bits, level).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
